cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you utilize THE MRIDANSH, the AETHER-MRID1607X computational engine, or its research artifacts in your scientific work, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "THE MRIDANSH: AETHER-MRID1607X Planetary Hydro-Terramorphic Engine"
abstract: >-
  THE MRIDANSH (AETHER-MRID1607X) is an aerospace-certified, physics-guided multi-modal
  Earth observation digital twin designed to estimate the vadose-zone state of soil
  from multi-spectral and synthetic aperture radar (SAR) satellite telemetry. Operating
  under RTCA DO-178C Level-A deterministic invariants, the system couples the nonlinear
  1D/2D Richards partial differential equation (PDE) with deep Physics-Informed Neural
  Networks (PINN), Ensemble Kalman Filtering (EnKF), and Saxton-Rawls pedotransfer models.
  The engine powers two downstream sovereign domains: precision Variable-Rate Irrigation
  (VRI) for smallholder farmer welfare in agronomy, and Meyerhof-Bekker terramechanics
  for heavy civil machine trafficability and slope liquefaction risk.
